Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.28.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.28.0 (archive 30): (1) touch/click death inside the panel after a few rapid resizes fixed at the root: FBScene.isValid flips NO for a single beat during layer-drop windows and the old guard killed itself on the first NO, leaving nobody to pull the scene back to contentState=2 (visible but non-interactive); isValid must now stay NO for 3 consecutive beats before the guard stops, transient NO beats are just skipped; (2) dead gestures while an app is foreground: 0.27 proved the status-bar window shares the main scene, so the fix moved to window arbitration - when no explicit windowLevel is configured the floating window now auto-raises to UIStatusBarWindow.windowLevel + 100 (the status bar window keeps touch routing over apps, Dynamic Island taps prove it); (3) the visually non-proportional resize (math was exact 0.535 AR all along) is the stretch of the presentationView while win.frame is ahead of scene.frame - the drag-time sync throttle is tightened 250ms -> 120ms to shrink the gap. 0.27.0 (archive 29): (1) not-running apps launch suspended:YES - Stheno's exact way - so nothing goes fullscreen first and the desktop stays visible behind the floating window (no more black background / manual back-to-home); (2) resize keeps showing LIVE content: during the gesture the snapshot pad is neither raised to the top nor left covering (it is lowered immediately), because the frequent layer drops during a drag made the frozen snapshot mask the real render; (3) corner radius 16 -> 24; (4) default floating window size is now Stheno-style tall card 0.55 x 0.72 of the screen, configurable via new defaultWidthScale / defaultHeightScale keys (cfgVersion 21); (5) the floating window now prefers the always-active UIStatusBarWindow scene (guessing the inactive-main-scene touch routing as the cause of dead gestures while an app is foreground; falls back to the main scene). 0.26.0: archive 28 fixes - (1) close/reload buttons were untouchable because their container had userInteractionEnabled=NO which kills the whole subtree's touches (container now left default); (2) hosted app corners are clipped with a 16 pt radius on the content area itself (window corner no longer covers the content since the trim ring was added); (3) the frozen-snapshot look during resize is gone: scene.frame is now throttled-synced (250 ms) while dragging so live content follows the finger; (4) launching a not-running app now uses UIApplication's private launchApplicationWithIdentifier:suspended:NO (the exact channel FrontBoardAppLauncher and Stheno use - FBSOpenApplicationService proved unusable: no +sharedInstance and no openApplication selector on instances). 0.25.0 reproduces Stheno's out-of-frame gesture model 1:1 (reverse-engineered from Stheno.dylib: cardTrim / EdgeBarControlView / PanGestureSubType / finalCardCorner): the window is now the content area plus an 18 pt invisible trim ring on all four sides; edges drag the window, corners resize it proportionally with the opposite corner pinned (incremental accumulation kept - the anchor is only used for origin derivation), a double tap anywhere on the trim toggles the app picker, and the hosted app receives every touch inside the content area like before. The old inner strips and the corner grip are gone; the reload/close buttons float small and translucent at the content's top-right. Also fixes archive 27: FBSOpenApplicationService has no +sharedInstance (unrecognized selector) - it is now created via alloc/init, so tapping a not-running app really launches it and auto-hosts 2 s later. No new config keys; cfgVersion stays 20.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
